  "worked_solution": "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(1)=\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(1)\\cdot g(1)-f(1)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(1)}{(g(1))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph above, we obtain that $f(1)=3$ and $g(1)=2.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (0,2)$ equals $1.$ So, ${f}^{\u2032}(1)=1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (0,3)$ equals $-1.$ So, ${g}^{\u2032}(1)=-1.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(1) & =\\frac{{f}^{\u2032}(1)\\cdot g(1)-f(1)\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(1)}{(g(1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
